      "problem": "If $X=\\{2,4,8\\}$, then $P(X)=$",
      "worked_solution": "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $∅.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14180007/assets/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n∅=\\{\\},\\,\\{2\\},\\,\\{4\\},\\,\\{8\\},\\,\\{2,4\\},\\,\\{2,8\\},\\,\\{4,8\\},\\,\\{2,4,8\\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)=\\{∅,\\{2\\},\\{4\\},\\{8\\},\\{2,4\\},\\{2,8\\},\\{4,8\\},\\{2,4,8\\}\\}.\n$$",
